      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Vik,' Max delivers a punchy one-word reaction built around the Russian word meaning 'Vika'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Походу, сработал твой план.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Looks like your plan worked.' Here Max anchors the line on the word meaning 'apparently' and builds the thought around 'worked' and 'plan'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Замолчи, пожалуйста.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Shut up, please.' Vika delivers a punchy one-word reaction built around the Russian word meaning 'to fall silent'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Это наш новый хозяин.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This is our new owner.' Russian omits the present-tense verb 'to be' here, linking 'new' directly with 'owner', combining 'new' with 'owner'. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
